        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పన్ను",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పన్ను (pannu) — \"a tooth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian pal. Tamil kept பல்; Kannada has ಹಲ್ಲು, with that p- to h- law working again exactly where the last chapter said to watch for it. Telugu took a third road, the -l- coming out as -n- and doubling."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An honest warning: పన్ను (pannu) is also the word for a tax. Nothing joins the tooth to the tax but an accident of sound. Telugu has a fair number of these pairs, and context is the only fix — which is what context is for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two: a leg and a tooth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pannu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pannu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "kālu, then pannu, and say which of the two also names something you pay",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *kālu*, then *pannu*, and say which of the two also names something you pay]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does పన్ను (pannu) mean? (\"a tooth\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
