        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: వేలు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వేలు (vēlu) — \"a finger\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian viral. Tamil kept விரல் entire; Kannada has ಬೆರಳು; Telugu dropped the -r- and came out with వేలు (vēlu). On the page the three look barely related, and they are the same word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is still working inside compounds: బొటనవేలు, the thumb, is the stubby one of the set."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. Note that చెయ్యి and వేలు (vēlu) are separate roots — Telugu does not build the finger out of the hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
