        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కడుపు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కడుపు (kaḍupu) — \"the stomach, the belly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కడుపు is the unfussy everyday word, and it carries the commonest way of saying you have eaten enough: kaḍupu niṇḍindi, \"the stomach has filled\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also says, gently and without ever being explicit, that a woman is expecting. Sanskrit's ఉదరం exists in Telugu and stays where the clinical register lives."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five more body words: a leg, a tooth, hair, a finger, a belly. With తల, చెయ్యి, కన్ను, ముక్కు, నోరు and చెవి behind them, you can point at most of a person."
            }
          ]
        },
